1
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,057
Liu clothing

2
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:17,140
has

3
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:22,630
been so much later

4
00:00:22,713 --> 00:00:29,220
for

5
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:30,710
Japanese

6
00:00:30,793 --> 00:00:31,623
anime

7
00:00:31,706 --> 00:00:32,536
for Japanese anime.

8
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,240
Whoa, where am I?

9
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,680
And why does everything look so huge?

10
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,360
Hey, that's cute.

11
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:21,228
It's some kind of robot
monkey or something.

12
00:01:21,340 --> 00:01:22,170
Hi.

13
00:01:22,740 --> 00:01:23,570
Huh?

14
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:24,810
Oh, no!

15
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:27,240
They made a monkey out of me!

16
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:31,480
Poor Tristan. Don't worry.

17
00:01:31,860 --> 00:01:35,357
The Big Five said they had him in
some kind of a virtual holding area.

18
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:38,897
We just have to find him before
they take control of his body.

19
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:39,810
That's right.

20
00:01:39,893 --> 00:01:42,237
And then his mind will be
trapped somewhere in cyberspace.

21
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,497
We gotta get him back.

22
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:44,410
Now!

23
00:01:54,160 --> 00:01:55,540
Hello, Kyla. Huh?

24
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:58,080
Look, Seto, it's Tristan.

25
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:00,160
Finally, friendly face.

26
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,914
Where's Yu-Gi and the rest of the gang?

27
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,480
Whoa, look out!

28
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:09,900
Tristan, what are you thinking?

29
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:12,240
My name's not Tristan.

30
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:14,780
And I'm thinking about revenge.

31
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:16,120
Who are you?

32
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:17,515
Your worst nightmare.

33
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,677
Look, it's Tristan!

34
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,760
And Kaiba! And Mokuba! Yugi!

35
00:02:29,200 --> 00:02:32,660
Tristan, I knew we'd track
you down, pal! Are you okay?

36
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,460
Why don't you kids run along?

37
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:37,720
Wait a sec!

38
00:02:37,980 --> 00:02:39,745
You're not Tristan, you phony!

39
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,588
What are you talking about?

40
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,604
Wait, Joey, I think he's right!

41
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,580
Yes, I've taken over your friend's body.

42
00:02:47,860 --> 00:02:52,320
And now that that's over, I
can take care of you! En garde!

43
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:57,160
Nice try!

44
00:02:57,420 --> 00:02:58,860
Why are you doing this?

45
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,920
Because you need to pay
for what you did to me.

46
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:04,690
Goodbye.

47
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:09,017
Wait, come back!

48
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,160
What is that?

49
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:15,460
This is getting too weird. Take that!

50
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:20,000
Joey, it's still his body!

51
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:22,950
Hello?

52
00:03:23,033 --> 00:03:23,863
Hello?

53
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,380
Pardon me!

54
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:29,930
Seto!

55
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:37,020
Kaiba, I've taken something from you,
so we're even now. Come back! Right now!

56
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:40,860
Too late! He's gone! Oh, no!

57
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,230
Mokuma!

58
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,617
What now, guys?

59
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,640
Kive is after the fake, Tristan.

60
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:54,217
So we gotta find out
where the real one is.

61
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:55,130
Joey's right.

62
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:56,790
Huh?

63
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,020
It's that robot runt again.

64
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,665
I don't trust this little rat.

65
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:05,820
He's a monkey, and how
dangerous can he really be?

66
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,697
Wait, don't touch it, Serenity.

67
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:10,357
For all we know, this
chimp could be a trap.

68
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,560
Good point, Duke.

69
00:04:11,860 --> 00:04:13,877
Maybe we should just take this guy apart.

70
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:17,431
Yeah, we could unscrew his head
and take out his batteries.

71
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,590
No way!

72
00:04:18,673 --> 00:04:20,679
Hey, don't you lay a finger on him.

73
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:22,377
What's the problem, Serenity?

74
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:25,166
This little guy risked
his life to save Kaiba.

75
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,937
I guess that's a good thing.

76
00:04:27,020 --> 00:04:28,780
And just look at him. Hi.

77
00:04:29,260 --> 00:04:30,360
He's adorable.

78
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,277
Just do me a favor, okay?

79
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:36,184
Keep that thing out of my face.

80
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,900
Okay, we gotta get going, guys.

81
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:44,281
The Big Five may have Tristan's body, but
his mind's gotta be around here somewhere.

82
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:46,090
Zippy!

83
00:04:46,173 --> 00:04:49,700
Hey, I got my eye on you, you
robot formants. Joey, stop!

84
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,440
Hang on, Mokuba.

85
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:55,602
I'll rescue you from these
corporate sleazeballs.

86
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:00,707
This shouldn't be too tough.

87
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,025
Hey, you, get out of the road!

88
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:22,200
So we meet again, Setokaba.

89
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,540
Who are you?

90
00:05:24,260 --> 00:05:27,240
How quickly we forget our old friends.

91
00:05:27,520 --> 00:05:28,360
Enough games.

92
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:30,180
Where can I find Mokuba?

93
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:35,481
If you ever want to see that brother of
yours again, you'll have to make it past me.

94
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,200
Stop right there, Nesbitt.

95
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:45,600
Yes, Noah? All right.

96
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:46,980
What's going on?

97
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,940
Well, sir, I've taken Seto's brother.

98
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:53,280
I can see that, but why
have you taken him? Simple.

99
00:05:53,580 --> 00:05:58,227
When I worked for Kaiba Corp, Seto took
everything from me, so this is payback.

100
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,437
That wasn't part of the deal, Nesbitt.

101
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,000
You've broken my rules.

102
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,065
But, sir, what are you saying?

103
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,580
Hand the boy to me.

104
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,940
I've been waiting to take
you down for a long time.

105
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,320
Bring it on.

106
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:19,920
Where am I?

107
00:06:20,120 --> 00:06:21,160
You're with me.

108
00:06:21,740 --> 00:06:22,570
Noah!

109
00:06:22,653 --> 00:06:23,940
Stay away from me!

110
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:28,280
Wait till Seto finds out! Seto? Ha!

111
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:31,760
He won't be rescuing you
anytime soon. That's not true!

112
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:34,357
My brother would never
let anything happen to me.

113
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,860
He's got his hands tied.

114
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,380
See for yourself.

115
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:40,490
Seto!

116
00:06:40,573 --> 00:06:43,817
He'll have to make it past
my associate to rescue you.

117
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:45,740
Is that one of the Big Five?

118
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:49,540
Do you have any idea
who you're dealing with?

119
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,880
Well, now I do.

120
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:54,620
It took me a minute, but I
recognize your voice, Lector.

121
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,240
So let's get this duel over with.

122
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:59,520
My sentiments exactly.

123
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:04,420
So go ahead and choose your deck
from the Virtual Cards database.

124
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:05,850
Gladly.

125
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:10,380
Now choose a monster to
act as your Deck Master.

126
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,820
This is a no-brainer, Lector.

127
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,700
I choose Lord of Dragons!

128
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:20,960
And I have already taken
the form of my Deckmaster.

129
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,534
Can you tell which monster I've become?

130
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:26,248
No, and quite frankly,
I don't care, Lecter.

131
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:31,280
Because crushing you will be a simple
task, regardless of your Deckmaster.

132
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:32,720
So let's begin!

133
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:36,160
It's time to duel, as they say.

134
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:39,120
Don't expect any courtesy from me.

135
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:40,700
I'll go first.

136
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:43,480
I play one monster in Defense Mode.

137
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:47,380
Then I'll place two cards
face down and end my turn.

138
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,020
I summon Spear Dragon.

139
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,560
You're so confident, aren't you, Mr. Cut?

140
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,620
Well, go ahead and attack me.

141
00:07:57,900 --> 00:08:02,300
My monster is in defense mode, so
my life points are well protected.

142
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,577
You're wrong, Lector.

143
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:05,307
You didn't do your research.

144
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:08,760
Spear Dragon, attack his face down card.

145
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:12,477
You've attacked Hero's Shadow Scout,

146
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:16,120
So you must draw three
cards and show them to me.

147
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,740
So what?

148
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:22,237
You still lose life points, even though
your monster was in defense mode,

149
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:24,757
thanks to my spear
dragon's special ability.

150
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:27,880
I told you, you didn't
do your research. Well,

151
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,877
you have to discard the two
magic cards you just drew,

152
00:08:30,960 --> 00:08:32,784
thanks to my monster's ability.

153
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,420
My move's not over.

154
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,840
I place one card face down.

155
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:42,580
When the time is right, I'll reveal my
crush card, and this duel will be over.

156
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,940
Say goodbye, you faceless fool.

157
00:08:45,580 --> 00:08:49,060
Before I take my turn, I'll
activate my track card.

158
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,520
Solemn wishes.

159
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:52,560
Now I'll draw.

160
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:58,700
And since my turn has officially
begun, my life points will increase.

161
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:01,877
That's because my Solemn
Wishes track card boosts

162
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:05,380
my power by 500 points
with every card I draw.

163
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:09,757
Enjoy it while you can, because
your next turn will be your last.

164
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,722
then you'll all pay for
taking my little brother.

165
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:19,320
Now I play a monster in defense mode and
place one card face down on the field.

166
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:20,760
Your move.

167
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,130
Strange.

168
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:25,057
He must see that my Spear
Dragon goes into defense mode

169
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:28,037
after it attacks and that
it has zero defense points.

170
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:30,260
So why didn't he attack it?

171
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:33,520
Is there a problem, Mr. Kaiba?

172
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,877
Because I'd appreciate
it if you'd make your

173
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:39,320
move so I can defeat you
and take over your body.

174
00:09:40,380 --> 00:09:43,460
In your dreams, I summon Giant Germ!

175
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:47,000
Then I'll switch my Spear
Dragon into attack mode!

176
00:09:47,360 --> 00:09:50,520
Now, Spear Dragon, destroy
his face-down monster!

177
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,760
Not so fast, Settles!

178
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,580
Activate Track Car!

179
00:09:55,060 --> 00:09:57,060
Mask of Complexity!

180
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,570
Ugh!

181
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:00,660
What is this?

182
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,320
I can hardly see!

183
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:03,761
That's the idea!

184
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:06,697
Now you won't know whose
monster you're attacking!

185
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:07,997
Mine or yours!

186
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,540
That's not fair.

187
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,640
Hmm, finally a duel worth watching.

188
00:10:12,880 --> 00:10:15,240
Time for you to attack, Mr. Kyber.

189
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:18,519
But I doubt you'll be able
to see what you're doing.

190
00:10:19,460 --> 00:10:22,280
Spear Dragon, attack that card.

191
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,580
Now take a look and
see what you've chosen.

192
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:31,740
Ah, too bad, Mr. Kyber.

193
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:35,640
It looks like you've attacked
your own monster, Giant Jer.

194
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,680
That's what I was aiming
for, you foolish old man.

195
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:46,360
I had to destroy my giant germ so I can
activate my all-powerful crush card trap.

196
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,960
It's destroyed, but how?

197
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:54,278
You have the power to destroy traps?

198
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:57,300
Now I know what monster you are, Lecter.

199
00:10:57,540 --> 00:11:01,200
The only monster I know with
the power to destroy trap cards.

200
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,277
Yes, I am Junzo.

201
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:08,417
And with a monster this powerful
as my Deathmaster You don't

202
00:11:08,500 --> 00:11:13,220
stand a chance So prepare to
lose your body to me Forever

203
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:20,857
I've been waiting for this
moment for quite some time, Mr.

204
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,917
Kyber For years I stood by and watched you

205
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,497
rise to power A power
that should have been mine

206
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:30,877
As your stepfather's right-hand man I not

207
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:34,360
only helped run Kyber
Corp I helped raise you.

208
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,240
And how did you repay me?

209
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,057
By taking away everything
I worked so hard to gain.

210
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:40,657
How did I do that, Lecter?

211
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:45,152
I was next in line to run the company
until you forced your way to the top.

212
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:47,242
I'll never forgive you for that.

213
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,600
All right, Seto.

214
00:11:49,780 --> 00:11:52,309
As of today, your formal
education is over.

215
00:11:52,580 --> 00:11:56,097
It's time for you to start
learning lessons in the real world.

216
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:58,121
Now I have something to give you.

217
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,753
I think you'll be quite pleased with it.

218
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:02,650
Hobson!

219
00:12:02,740 --> 00:12:05,620
Present Seto with his gift of $10,000,000.

220
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:09,320
Relax, you two.

221
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,857
Everything in life comes at a price,

222
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:14,940
so if you think I'm just
handing this money to you,

223
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,340
then think again.

224
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:21,660
I am lending you this small
fortune as a test. A test?

225
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:22,800
That's right.

226
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:27,200
You have exactly one year to return
the money to me. Is that clear?

227
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:30,837
But you must pay me ten
times that amount next year.

228
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,940
If you pass this test,

229
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,897
you will prove to me you have the business

230
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:37,660
skills necessary to call yourself a Kaiba.

231
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:41,120
This is all explained
in your contract, Seto.

232
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:44,160
Pass and you earn the last name Kaiba.

233
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,540
Fail and it's back to
the orphanage. I accept.

234
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:52,697
Now that's a very wise
decision on your part.

235
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:56,074
My assistant lector is the
only one allowed to help you.

236
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:59,180
You have one year to pass.

237
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,597
What are you going to do, Seto?

238
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:08,620
I mean, turning $10 million into $100
million in only one year seems impossible.

239
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:09,940
Hey, don't worry.

240
00:13:10,200 --> 00:13:12,259
See, business is just another game.

241
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,837
Look, there are a hundred
cards here, right?

242
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:18,660
Now pretend each card represents
a piece of a company. Yeah?

243
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:21,517
Well, this is where it all becomes a game.

244
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:24,424
The trick is to own more
cards than anyone else.

245
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:27,197
If you can do that, you'll
control the company.

246
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,517
And how many cards do you need to do that?

247
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,680
The magic number is 51.

248
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:37,560
No one else can ever have more cards than
you as long as you own 51 out of 100.

249
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,040
That's how you win.

250
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:40,700
Hey, Lecter,

251
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:46,440
I need you to spend all $10 million of
my money and buy me 51 % of a company.

252
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,320
What kind of company, sir?

253
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:51,400
Any kind, as long as
they value their workers.

254
00:13:54,560 --> 00:13:55,400
Come in.

255
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:58,960
Sir, I found and purchased
the perfect company.

256
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:00,350
Hmm.

257
00:14:00,433 --> 00:14:04,920
This company is known for treating
its employees like family. How cool!

258
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:06,520
Your very own company.

259
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,857
Is it going to make you
all the money you need?

260
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:10,017
That's a good question.

261
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:12,177
You see, this company
doesn't make much money.

262
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:17,360
But there is a way that I can use this
company to get what I need right now.

263
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:20,460
Force the president to
run the company my way.

264
00:14:22,660 --> 00:14:23,490
What?

265
00:14:23,573 --> 00:14:26,537
Why should I buy the company
back at ten times the price?

266
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:31,561
Because if you don't, I'll shut this place
down, leaving all your employees jobless.

267
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:35,120
You are horrible, and you
leave me with no choice.

268
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:39,564
With my help, you made ten times
your money back in that one day.

269
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,300
And you got all the credit.

270
00:14:41,500 --> 00:14:42,441
Well, of course.

271
00:14:42,580 --> 00:14:46,109
It was my business skills that
earned me that money, Lecter.

272
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,280
All you did was follow orders.

273
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,460
That's all you were good for.

274
00:14:50,720 --> 00:14:52,940
You never once had your own idea.

275
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,237
You couldn't have run Kaiba Corp.

276
00:14:55,320 --> 00:15:00,260
Not only could I, but I will, once I
escape to the real world in your body.

277
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,270
Not quite.

278
00:15:01,353 --> 00:15:05,500
When my giant germ was destroyed,
its special ability was activated,

279
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:07,720
allowing me to summon another one.

280
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:11,440
You're just delaying your
eventual destruction, Mr. Kaiba.

281
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:15,994
Since I've assumed the form of Jinzo,
all of your trap cards are useless.

282
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:21,220
And you know as well as I do that no
one wins a duel with monsters alone.

283
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,657
Lecter, I'll never lose this game to you.

284
00:15:24,740 --> 00:15:28,160
Oh, you'll lose so much
more than just this game.

285
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:33,480
Let the Onslaught continue. Remember,

286
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:38,980
I get 500 extra life points each draw
thanks to my Solemn Wishes trap card.

287
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:42,820
And now I'll place two
cards face down. Whatever.

288
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:50,180
Spear Dragon, attack his face
down monster with Cyclone Blast.

289
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,440
Nice try.

290
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:59,180
But I'm afraid your attack is
useless, because I activate Cyber Jar,

291
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:03,360
which destroys every
monster on the field. Oh no!

292
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:15,340
It may have cost me a few life points,
but it cost you all of your monsters.

293
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:19,080
Now we draw five cards and
summon any monsters we pick.

294
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:21,580
Force Raider and Twin-Headed Behemoth.

295
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,397
Injection Fairy Lily.

296
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:25,500
So they both start over.

297
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,680
Go, Seto!

298
00:16:27,020 --> 00:16:28,726
And since it's my turn again,

299
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:33,600
I gain another 500 life points
thanks to my Solemn Wishes trap card.

300
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:37,180
And now I activate Watch Tranquilizer.

301
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:43,097
This magic card equips me
with an electronic device that

302
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:46,077
lowers the attack strength
of your offensive monsters,

303
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:46,990
Mr. Kaiba.

304
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:51,240
Let's give it a test run, shall we?

305
00:16:56,220 --> 00:17:01,717
my watch tranquilizer is about to weaken
your force raider since it's a level 4

306
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:08,217
monster it will lose 400 attack points
bringing it down to a total of 1500 that

307
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:13,997
doesn't matter his fairy lily is still
weaker than my monster now it's time for

308
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:19,860
you to experience my fairy lily's special
ability By giving up 2,000 life points,

309
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,480
I can raise her power by 3,000.

310
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:25,960
Enough to wipe out your
monster and then serve.

311
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,580
Lily, attack!

312
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:36,540
And that's not all, Mr. Kyber.

313
00:17:37,780 --> 00:17:39,520
Activate Semic's Blessing.

314
00:17:40,760 --> 00:17:43,337
This magic card allows me to take the life

315
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:46,277
points that you just lost
and add them to my own.

316
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:49,920
Reducing your chances
of survival even more

317
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:51,590
Finally,

318
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:57,657
I'll summon a monster in defense mode
and end my turn Very well You'll never

319
00:17:57,740 --> 00:18:02,397
recuperate from the blow I just delivered
I've conquered every challenge life

320
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:07,837
has given me This duel will be no
different I'll place one monster in defense

321
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:12,857
mode So you thought you'd play it safe
by summoning a monster in defense mode?

322
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:16,320
Well, I have other plans
for you, Mr. Kaiba.

323
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,460
Activate Life-Absorbing Machine.

324
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:22,737
This trap card allows
me to reclaim half of

325
00:18:22,820 --> 00:18:25,291
the life points I gave up in my last turn,

326
00:18:25,520 --> 00:18:27,440
giving me quite a power boost.

327
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:32,980
Not that I need extra life points to
ensure my victory, but it couldn't hurt.

328
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:43,280
Next, I'll sacrifice my face-down monster
in order to summon my ultimate weapon.

329
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,860
Whoa, what's that?

330
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:57,140
Good thing we found this
virtual pickup truck.

331
00:18:57,380 --> 00:18:59,677
Yeah, it beats walking, that's for sure.

332
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:01,878
And it should help us to find the...

333
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:07,558
Hey, why'd you stop the truck, Joey?

334
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,920
Look, Hugh, what is that?

335
00:19:11,360 --> 00:19:12,440
Oh, wow!

336
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:14,860
It looks like some kind of rocket.

337
00:19:29,380 --> 00:19:32,500
Now deploying communication center.

338
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:47,080
Activating Infrared Sighting Beam.

339
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:50,640
Searching for pre-programmed target.

340
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,600
Seto Kaiba Located.

341
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:55,380
Set for Destruction.
